Item 15 (the control panel and windows) is done and the gate passes: 2557 Racket tests, the 105 new GUI tests, and the Chez checks. `chez_scheme/original/` and `tests/golden/` are untouched. Nothing is committed.

**One thing you should know first.** Your session sets `WAYLAND_DISPLAY`, and with it GTK ignores Xvfb. So my first three scratch GUI runs, a few seconds each, opened windows on your real screen before I noticed. Every GUI run now goes through `env -u WAYLAND_DISPLAY GDK_BACKEND=x11 xvfb-run` (in `tests/run-tests.sh` and the command in CLAUDE.md), and the GUI test refuses to start if `WAYLAND_DISPLAY` is set. It's logged in `docs/anomalies_and_quirks.md` and in my memory notes.

**What exists now**
- `racket racket/main.rkt` opens the control panel and every Metacat window as frames tiled on the screen. The control panel has the problem entry, Step/Go/Stop/Reset, the speed slider, and the Help, Demos, Windows, Options and Memory menus (Save commentary to file is under Options).
- `gui.ss` is ported as `racket/gui/gui.rktl`. The button actions, the control panel's messages and the window controllers are copied from the original. The widgets themselves had to be rewritten for racket/gui.
- The engine runs in its own thread, standing in for the original's REPL thread. The panel hands it work; each job runs until the model stops itself.
- `demos.ss` is ported too, because the Demos menu needs it. Item 16 now only needs its tests.

**Tests** (`racket/gui-tests/control-panel-test.rkt`, about 9 s on Xvfb, in the gate). It clicks the panel's real widgets. Every run driven this way ends at the golden's codelet count and random-generator state:
- a full run (395 codelets);
- a run in step mode, with the step size set through the Options dialog;
- a run stopped at a breakpoint and resumed by clicking the Workspace;
- run 7 (2170 codelets) stopped with Stop, resumed with Go, and run again after Reset.

It also covers Save commentary, Clear Memory, showing and hiding windows, self-watching off and on, resizing a window, and a Demos item. Five of six deliberate breakages of the GUI code were caught; the sixth changes nothing, because the command line gets cleared again anyway.

The tests were not written first: a scratch script drove the first runs and found two of the bugs below, and the test came after.

**Bugs found and fixed**
- My stand-in for SWL's message queue could freeze the GUI thread.
- A scrollbar appearing after layout covered the right edge of the Commentary text.
- The original has one resize queue for all windows and keeps only the last of simultaneous resizes. At startup several windows resized at once, so the Commentary never redrew.

**Screenshots.** I captured the whole virtual screen with `tests/gui-screenshot.rkt`. At codelet 513 of `abc abd mrrjjj` the Workspace matches item 13's offscreen picture. Run 7's `wyz` screen shows the commentary wrapped and scrolled to the newest paragraph, plus the Trace's snag and clamp events. One layout issue remains: the Vertical Themes window ends about 30 px below the bottom of a 1200 px screen.

**Differences from the original** (in `docs/divergences.md`)
- racket/gui can't colour native widgets or set fonts on menu items, so highlighted menu items are shown as checked instead.
- Help and Clear Memory are in their own menus, because racket/gui's menu bar holds only menus.
- The original left window placement to the window manager; the port tiles the windows itself.
- The item's "Run" and "Pause" are the original's Go and Stop. I kept its four buttons.

**Not tested:** clamping a theme pattern (Options ▸ Clamp theme pattern) is ported but has no automated test yet.

PROGRESS.md (now 16/18) and iterations.md are updated.

# result: success in 2421s, 108 turns, cost $9.40
